<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39128" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιδᾰπᾰν-τικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fit for displaying</i> or
				<i>showing off</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤθους καὶ πάθους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Salt.</u>
					35
				</span></i>
			; ἡ
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιδεικτική</span>
			<i>display</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Sph.</u>
				224b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. λόγοι</span> speeches <i>for display</i>,
				<i>set</i> orations, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				61.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. γένος λόγων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1358b8
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἐ</span>. <i>declamatory</i>
			speaker, ib.<i><span class="en">
				1359a15
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Comp.Dem.Cic.</u>
				1
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς, πολεμεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Luc.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					4.11
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερον, γράφε ν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.28e
				</span></i>
			.</div>
